<p class="risk wrap">Every dental treatment carries some risk, and results vary from person to person. Your dentist will explain the benefits, risks and alternatives before any treatment begins.</p>
<section class="dbody land-body">
  <div class="wrap dbody__in">
    <div>
      <h2 data-reveal>What is a dental check-up?</h2><p data-reveal>A check-up is a full look at your mouth. The dentist checks each tooth for decay, looks at your gums, and checks any old fillings, crowns or bridges. They also look at your bite and the soft tissue inside your mouth.</p><p data-reveal>If needed, the dentist may suggest a dental X-ray. An X-ray shows areas that are hidden between the teeth or under the gums. After the check-up, the dentist tells you what they found. If you need treatment, they explain the options, the cost and what each one involves. You decide what to do next.</p>
      <h2 class="land-h2" data-reveal>Who is it for?</h2><p data-reveal>A check-up is for anyone who wants to keep their teeth and gums healthy. It is useful if you have not seen a dentist for some time, if you have pain or sensitivity, or if your gums bleed when you brush. It is also a good first step if you are new to Dubai and need a dentist near you.</p><p data-reveal>Many people book a check-up every six months. Your dentist will tell you how often you should come. Children can have check-ups too. See <a class="link-u" href="kids-dentist-deira.html">dental care for kids</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="dfocus">
      <figure class="land-pic" data-reveal><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="../assets/img/treatments/general-600.webp?v=15 600w, ../assets/img/treatments/general-1200.webp?v=15 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 48em) 92vw, 520px"><img src="../assets/img/treatments/general-1200.jpg?v=15" srcset="../assets/img/treatments/general-600.jpg?v=15 600w, ../assets/img/treatments/general-1200.jpg?v=15 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 48em) 92vw, 520px" alt="Dental Check-up in Deira at Pearlecent, Al Rigga" width="1200" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture></figure>
      <h2 data-reveal>How the visit works</h2>
      <ol class="land-steps" data-reveal><li><span>Book a time online, by chat or by phone.</span></li><li><span>At reception, we take your details and ask about your health and any medicines you take.</span></li><li><span>The dentist checks your teeth and gums, and may suggest an X-ray.</span></li><li><span>The dentist explains what they found and answers your questions.</span></li><li><span>If you need treatment, we book another visit at a time that suits you.</span></li></ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="dbody land-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <div class="wrap land-faq__in">
    <div>
      <h2 id="faq-h" data-reveal>Questions about dental check-up</h2>
      <div class="faq"><details data-reveal><summary>Is the first check-up free?</summary><p>Yes. Your first general dental consultation at Pearlecent is free. If you need an X-ray or any treatment, the dentist tells you the cost before anything is done.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>What should I bring?</summary><p>Bring a photo ID and a list of any medicines you take. If you have dental insurance, ask our team about it when you book.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>Do I need a cleaning as well?</summary><p>Many people have a cleaning at the same time as their check-up. The dentist will tell you if you need one. Read more about <a class="link-u" href="teeth-cleaning-deira.html">teeth cleaning</a>.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>When is the clinic open?</summary><p>We are open Saturday to Thursday from 9 AM to 10 PM, and on Friday from 1 PM to 9 PM.</p></details></div>
    </div>
    <div class="land-visit" data-reveal>
      <h2>Visiting Pearlecent in Al Rigga</h2>
      <p>Pearlecent Shifah Medical Center is a family dental clinic in Deira, open since 2018. You can find us in Room 104, on the first floor of the Al Zarooni Building, 73 Al Rigga Road.</p>
      <p>We are open Saturday to Thursday from 9 AM to 10 PM, and on Friday from 1 PM to 9 PM. Your first general dental consultation is free. You can split your payment into 4 with Tabby or Tamara.</p>
      <p>Before any treatment, your dentist explains the benefits, the risks, the other options and the cost. You can ask questions and take time to decide.</p>
      <p><a class="link-u" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/LxxALHqsNsGpUrj29" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get directions</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
